ld be the worker size or how  many workers i want or how many cores i  want in each process and that's it now  you start your jupiter server you start  your task cluster  and you land into the very familiar page  which is jupiter labs  so  here  you will be just importing the saturn  cluster class  and then associating your task with  saturn cluster and you don't need to use  any other attributes or anything because  your dash clusters are already ready in  just a few clicks  so here on my right hand side you can  see the information  it will show you the dash dashboard you  can see how much memory you have or what  other workers you have  so task dashboards  are  um  very imp they are quite interesting if  you want to see uh how the workers are  behaving  and  how  much are you utilizing in all these  workers so this is how a das dashboard  looks like it will show you how are you  using the workers in the most optimal  way or can you make some changes so if  you look at the  oscar thread and each rectangle that you  see in that stream that is a task so  each task has a color for itself and the  white part that you see in between that  means that at this time  the worker is idle um if you look at the  progress which is at the bottom again  the color coding is same here and it  tells you that how is the progress for  each task  and the gray part that you see there it  tells you that the task is ready to run  so this will really help you analyze  that how are tasks being done by all the  workers  on the left hand side at the top you can  also see that how much memory is  consumed by each worker  so  if you see the 6.76 gb that is the total  memory being utilized by all the workers  this is like just one example there um  there are four other dashboards that you  can see  okay  now let's  check some examples to understand that  how powerful dusk is  so the first one is hyper parameter  tuning  um  on my left hand side  i have two codes where i'm doing hyper  parameter 